    {
      "obligation": "refuter:6:1",
      "id": "thm-fejer-convergence-in-lp",
      "location": "1.3",
      "defect": "unlicensed-inference",
      "evidence": "The step says, “Then \\(h\\in C_c((0,1))\\)” and that “exactly one summand is nonzero at each \\(x\\).” But [L4] supplies only \\(g\\in C_c(\\mathbb R)\\), while \\(\\eta_a\\) is merely linear on \\([0,a]\\) and \\([1-a,1]\\); it need not vanish on a neighbourhood of either endpoint. Thus a permitted \\(g\\) nonzero arbitrarily close to 0 yields \\(0\\in\\operatorname{supp}(h)\\), so \\(h\\) need not lie in \\(C_c((0,1))\\). Independently, at every integer all terms \\(h(x-m)\\) vanish, contradicting “exactly one summand.” A cutoff supported strictly inside \\((0,1)\\), or an at-most-one-summand argument with the endpoint values handled separately, repairs the periodization conclusion.",
      "severity": "nonfatal",
